# Git safety before resting

After substantial edits to this portfolio, **commit to git** before you finish your reply. Staged-only changes and unsaved editor buffers are not a backup.

## When to commit

Commit when you have changed any of:

- `src/**`, `public/**`, config files (`next.config.*`, `tailwind.config.*`, `package.json`)
- New interactive demos, modal components, or content schema updates

Skip only if: no file changes, or the user explicitly said not to commit.

## What to run (project root: `aaron_portfolio_2026/`)

After build + preview succeed (see `verify-build-before-resting.mdc`):

```bash
git status
git add <relevant paths>
git commit -m "descriptive message"
git status
```

## Rules

- Do **not** leave recovery-sized work only in the git index without a commit
- Do **not** commit secrets (`.env`, credentials)
- Do **not** amend or force-push unless the user explicitly asks
- Prefer one clear commit message describing **why** (e.g. recovery snapshot, new interactive demo)

